From 6ebd8c6a1213fcf56dd6144fcc8d5840f84b4e45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 091/206] drm/panel: Add Visionox VTDR6126 panel driver

Add a driver for the Visionox VTDR6126, as used in the Jolla Phone
(JP2601). The init sequence, power sequencing and timings come from the
vendor kernel's driver:

- vddio, 5 ms, vsn, 5 ms, vsp, 10 ms, then reset high/low/high with
  20 ms steps; the reverse to power off.
- DSC 1.1, 10 bits per component in, 8 bits per pixel out, two 516x8
  slices per line. The PPS goes to the panel as DCS 70h, and the same
  parameters are handed to the host encoder in full, so both ends agree
  on the rate-control setup rather than the host deriving its own.
- One 336.839 MHz line clock for both refresh rates: 60 Hz has a 2336
  line vertical front porch, 90 Hz a 792 line one, and DCS 6Ch selects
  the panel's 60 or 90 Hz mode. A DRM panel cannot see the mode at
  prepare time, so the rate is a module parameter and only that mode is
  offered.
- Brightness is the 12-bit DCS 51h.

Reset is taken as-is at probe, since the bootloader leaves the panel
running.
